; A page that embeds itself, twice. Each copy is drawn at 0.4 of its size,
; which lays it out about as wide as the page around it: wide enough that
; the site's layout gives it the same 720 pixel column. So every copy looks
; just like the page, however deep, and zooming in can go on forever. The
; browser stops loading copies once they're too small to see, and loads more
; as zooming makes them bigger.

(eval `(do ,@(source "site.sx")))

(demo "Fractal"
  "Both frames below load fractal.sx, the file that defines this page. Hold Ctrl and scroll over one to zoom in: it goes on forever."
  (row
    (frame :src "fractal.sx" :scale 0.4)
    (frame :src "fractal.sx" :scale 0.4)))
